Context()->texStrings;
BEGIN_TEXT
Let \( T \) be the solid tetrahedron in \( \mathbb{R}^3 \) with vertices \( (1,0,0), (0,1,0) \) and \( (0,0,1). \) $BR
 	Calculate the flux of the force \( F(x,y,z) = (x+z,x+y+2z,z + xy) \) outward through the three sides of \( T \) lying in the coordinate planes: \(xy\)-plane, \(yz\)-plane, and \(xz\)-plane.  You may give an exact answer or round to two decimal places.

$BR
\{$q1->ans_rule\}

END_TEXT
Context()->normalStrings;

##############################################################
#
#  Answers
#
#

ANS($q1->with(tolerance=>.015)->cmp);


# default tolerance is .01 or one percent.


ENDDOCUMENT();        